  ok   -- a 5-turn window reads FEWER bytes than the full file (4783 < 34308) -- the cost claim, in the control rather than only in the prose

the resume cursor: two windowed reads across an append == one full read
  ok   -- an unchanged file returns grew=False and an empty window
  ok   -- every flag on that empty window is UNMEASURED, not a clean result
  ok   -- after appending 4 turns the resumed read sees exactly those 4 (saw 4)
  ok   -- and it read 2263 bytes, not the whole 7922-byte file
  ok   -- a full read of the grown file sees all 14 turns, so nothing was lost at the seam
  ok   -- an offset past EOF sets rotated=True and falls back to a FULL read, rather than reporting an empty window for a replaced file

the `since` window
  ok   -- since=00:08 over turns stamped 00:00..00:11 keeps 4 turns (kept 4)
  ok   -- a `since` older than the file keeps every turn (kept 12)
  ok   -- and it is NOT reported as a local-span window, because it threw nothing away
  ok   -- a `since` in the future keeps no turn (kept 0), rather than defaulting to all
  ok   -- all three of these READS start at byte 0 (the file is smaller than the chunk), so only the TRIM can set the floor flag
  ok   -- and it is set for BOTH windowing modes and not for the full read -- the floor warning cannot be suppressed by a file being small

batchable_bash: fires on mergeable pairs, silent on dependent ones
  ok   -- POSITIVE: 8 self-contained Bash turns -> 7 mergeable pairs of 7 examined, FIRED
  ok   -- NEGATIVE: the same chain with alm#831's witness signature -> 0 of 7 pairs mergeable, not fired
  ok   -- BOUNDARY: measure 7 does not fire at threshold 7 and does at 6 (strictly greater, same rule as compute_flags)
  ok   -- the independent arm's pairs are accepted on their own merits: highest command-similarity 0.00, under the 0.60 retry threshold, so they were not merely not-retries
  ok   -- and the dependent arm is rejected by the WITNESS test, not the retry test: all 7 pairs have similarity < 0.60 AND at least one witness
  ok   -- no threshold -> NOT COMPUTED, with the count still reported
  ok   -- a window with no Bash pair at all -> UNMEASURED, not a clean zero
  ok   -- control 7: no raw command text reached an evidence row (0 leaks)

repeated_invocations: fires on a run, silent on distinct calls
  ok   -- POSITIVE: 9 identical Read calls -> consecutive run of 9, measure 9, FIRED
  ok   -- NEGATIVE: 9 all-different Bash calls -> 0 repeat rows, a MEASURED clean result
  ok   -- BOUNDARY: a run of 9 does not fire at threshold 9 and does at 8 -- and the threshold is compared against the RUN LENGTH, which is what signal 2 means by it, not against the number of groups
  ok   -- a 4-turn window sees a run of 4, not 9 -- the floor the note promises, measured
  ok   -- an empty file -> UNMEASURED and fired=False, which means NOTHING
  ok   -- a turn that called no tool -> UNMEASURED ('nothing to look at', not 'no repeats')

agent_reuse_gap: fires on delegable content, silent on orchestration
  ok   -- POSITIVE: 12 CONTENT turns, no dispatch -> gap at least 12, longest run 12, FIRED
  ok   -- NEGATIVE (the one that matters): 12 ORCHESTRATION turns -- the SAME 12-turn gap -- not fired, because alm#833 says those turns structurally cannot move
  ok   -- NEGATIVE: a dispatch at turn 10 of 12 -> gap of 1, not fired
  ok   -- BOUNDARY: a gap of 12 does not fire at threshold 12 and does at 11
  ok   -- raising min_content_run to 99 makes the same window not delegable-looking, so the long gap alone does not fire -- both halves are load-bearing
  ok   -- no threshold -> NOT COMPUTED, with the gap still reported
  ok   -- a FULL read reports its gap exactly (12), a WINDOWED read reports it as a floor (at least 6) -- because only the latter can be hiding an older dispatch

